Command Code: advertise each model's real --effort levels.

Patch 0003 showed a Reasoning picker on every Command Code model with the
full CLI set (low/medium/high/xhigh/max). The install's catalog is narrower
than that: DeepSeek is high/max, Qwen 3.8 is low/medium/xhigh, and models
whose Efforts cell is an em dash (Haiku, Kimi K2.7, ...) pick their own
depth. --list-models does not print those sets.

Read the Efforts column from the CLI's bundled models.md (next to the
binary, or COMMAND_CODE_PROXY_MODELS_CATALOG), merge BYOK reasoningEfforts
from ~/.commandcode/providers.json, and attach only that model's levels.
Models with no catalogued efforts keep capabilities null so the composer
hides the control instead of offering levels the CLI will reject.

